From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: aiueo52 <aiueo52@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 10:52:19 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 005/105] fix(qsa): size the pending index-key ring for the
 speculative verify window

The per-request pending ring was addressed by position % compress_ratio with a
ring of exactly one group. A chain verify window of W tokens writes W ring entries
in one forward, so any group completing inside the window aliased its members
(only L % ratio == 0 was correct at W=4). Size the ring as
R = ratio * (ceil(Wmax / ratio) + 1) (>= ratio + Wmax - 1) from the runtime maximum
draft-token count, thread ring_size through the metadata builders, the Triton graph
metadata kernel (RING constexpr) and the backend guard, and map padding rows to the
reserved request slot 0 on the host fallback path. No CUDA kernel changes.

Implemented by Codex (gpt-5.6-sol high) from a supervisor spec; CPU tests added.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
